@* Practice 1: the fallback page. This is an ordinary routed page, NOT a <Router> template.
   UseStatusCodePagesWithReExecute in Program.cs re-runs the pipeline against this URL whenever
   routing finds no endpoint for what the user typed, keeping the 404 status code.
   Because it's a normal page, it picks up MainLayout from DefaultLayout — the navbar comes
   along for free, and no <LayoutView> wrapper is needed. *@
@page "/not-found"

<PageTitle>Page Not Found</PageTitle>

<div class="alert alert-warning mt-4">
    <h3>Page Not Found</h3>
    <p>The page you requested does not exist.</p>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Go Home</a>
</div>
